Source and scope
================

This packaging targets Debian unstable and upstream tag v1.3.0, commit
9f810aefe9d3a59bbd97583631bc5e5de67e8301. The initial upload closes ITP
#1149848. The changelog remains UNRELEASED while the package is under review.

The Debian patch updates Ratatui/Crossterm to the versions available in
unstable, adapts the terminal error conversion and removes unused development
dependencies. Upstream files in the Git checkout are not modified.

dh-cargo builds offline against /usr/share/cargo/registry. It regenerates
Cargo.lock for Debian's dependency versions; debian/rules preserves and
restores the upstream lockfile on clean. No vendored crates are included.

Generate an unsigned source package
===================================

Run from the repository root, with an empty target/debian-source directory:

  mkdir -p target/debian-source
  git archive --format=tar --prefix=systemd-manager-tui-1.3.0/ v1.3.0 | \
    gzip -n > target/debian-source/systemd-manager-tui_1.3.0.orig.tar.gz
  tar -xzf target/debian-source/systemd-manager-tui_1.3.0.orig.tar.gz \
    -C target/debian-source
  cp -a debian target/debian-source/systemd-manager-tui-1.3.0/
  (cd target/debian-source && \
    dpkg-source --before-build systemd-manager-tui-1.3.0 && \
    dpkg-source -b systemd-manager-tui-1.3.0)

Validate
========

With an unstable sbuild environment already configured:

  sbuild --dist=unstable --arch=amd64 \
    target/debian-source/systemd-manager-tui_1.3.0-1.dsc

Run Lintian on the resulting .changes and autopkgtest against a disposable
unstable testbed. The CLI autopkgtest is deliberately marked superficial:
it verifies the installed executable without requiring a running systemd.
The normal build runs the unit suite. Eight integration tests are ignored
there because they need running system and user systemd managers; the
upstream CI runs those separately.

An interactive test must additionally cover service listing and operations
in a systemd-based VM. No upload, signing or RFS submission is automated by
this packaging.
